    tut:[{h:"Read the challenge",p:"A scale, a chord or a progression appears with a countdown. Picture the notes in your head before the bar runs out."},
         {h:"Pick and set up",p:"Before each game, pick the scale or chord as a card, then the timer and your helps. “Show the notes” shows the note names, “Light up the keys” shows where to play, and “Step-by-step help” gives nothing at first, then a hint every 8 s; the notes you find stay lit and a card builds up to help you remember them. Less help = more XP."},
         {h:"Play it on your piano",p:"Scales from the root up to the octave, chords from their lowest note, progressions chord by chord. Digital piano (MIDI), acoustic piano (mic) or on-screen keys: each correct note fills a box. MIDI works in Chrome and Edge (not in Safari)."},
         {h:"Time's up: the answer",p:"The answer lights up in blue and plays. Press Continue to move on, or Retry to try the same one again right away."},
         {h:"Level up and unlock",p:"Each perfect run fills a gauge: 3 steps unlock the next key, and each level opens new content. The Ear tab works without a piano: listen and pick the answer."}],
